<title>CROATIA: Croatia Sept retail prices up 0.1 pct, 3.1 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Croatia Sept retail prices up 0.1 pct, 3.1 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bureau of Statistics issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA RETAIL PRICES    SEPTEMBER  JAN-SEPT  AUGUST  SEPT '95</p>
<p> Monthly change (pct)	  +0.1	 --	 0.0     +1.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year		    +3.1	+3.5     +4.7     +2.9</p>
<p>NOTES -- Between January and August goods prices rose 2.5 percent and services 8.6 percent. Croatia introduced a radical anti-inflation programme in October 1993, when monthly inflation hit 38.7 percent. -- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
